              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">25-30%</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Discount that makes a real deal</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="when" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. When Do Black Friday Protein Powder Deals Start in 2026?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Most retailers start Black Friday pricing in the week of Thanksgiving, which in 2026 is Thursday, November 26, and run through Cyber Monday on November 30. Many brand sites open early-access or sitewide sales in the days before, and some extend them into the following week. There is no single start time, so the practical approach is to set your target prices now and check them each day from Monday, November 23.
          </p>

          <p>
            Big retailers and brand sites behave differently. Amazon, Target and Walmart tend to discount individual tubs by a fixed percentage or with a price cut on the listing, often on the best-known brands and the larger sizes. Brand sites more often run a sitewide percentage off with a code, sometimes stacked with free shipping or a free shaker. Supplement chains such as The Vitamin Shoppe and GNC usually push multi-buy offers and member pricing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Cyber Monday is often as good as Black Friday for protein, and sometimes better on brand sites, because many direct-to-consumer brands treat it as their main event. If a tub you want hits your target on Friday, buy it; if it is close but not there, it is reasonable to wait until Monday. Prices rarely fall further in the first week of December, although January sales can come close.
          </p>

          <p>
            One timing note: Amazon Subscribe and Save charges the price on the day an order ships, not the day you set it up. If you have a subscription due around the holiday, check whether the Black Friday price will apply to that shipment or whether a one-time purchase is cheaper.
          </p>
        </div>

