          <p>
            Some types already have products that beat the good-deal threshold at their normal price: Naked Pea at $0.71 per 25 g, NOW Sports Pea at about $1.02, Equate whey at $0.94 and Muscle Milk Pro Series at $1.25. For those, a Black Friday discount is a bonus rather than the reason to buy. For premium types such as hydrolyzed whey and organic plant blends, a sale is often the only time the price is reasonable.
          </p>

          <p>
            To check a deal, divide the sale price by the number of servings, divide that by the grams of protein per serving, and multiply by 25. A 5 lb tub at $99 with 74 servings of 24 g works out to $99 / 74 = $1.34 a serving, then $1.34 / 24 x 25 = $1.39 per 25 g: a decent price for a whey blend, not quite a great one. Our <a href="/tools/protein-cost-calculator/">protein cost calculator</a> does the arithmetic for you.
          </p>

          <p>
            Per serving, the same thresholds work out roughly as follows for a typical 24 to 25 g scoop: under about $1.30 a serving is a good Black Friday price for whey, under about $1.65 for whey isolate, and under about $1.25 for plain pea. For the full picture of normal prices by type, see our guide to <a href="/how-much-does-protein-powder-cost/">how much protein powder costs</a>.
          </p>
